{
  "_comment": [
    "Translates a legacy numbered block state from an imported build file into a",
    "block this game has. Read by src/schematic/mc_palette.cpp. The first number",
    "is the pre-flattening block id; the second is its 4-bit data value",
    "(orientation, species, colour), which is what most of the entries here exist",
    "to disambiguate.",
    "",
    "Row keys:",
    "  id          the legacy block id (required)",
    "  block       what EVERY data value of that id becomes (the row default)",
    "  variants    per-data-value overrides, written out or naming a set from",
    "              \"variant_sets\" below; a value mapped to null is skipped",
    "  family      the block a set's \"{family}\" placeholder expands to",
    "  skip        true when we have no block for it and it is dropped",
    "  substitute  true when the target is a stand-in, not the same block",
    "  fluid       true when the target is a liquid",
    "  note        why, for whoever reads this next",
    "",
    "Policy, so the entries below are not arbitrary: a full opaque cube we do not",
    "have becomes a full cube (stone, cobblestone, snow) so the structure stays",
    "solid, while a partial or decorative shape (torch, sign, pane, carpet,",
    "trapdoor, flower) is skipped, because inventing geometry reads worse than a",
    "gap and the report lists every skipped state with its count. An id with no",
    "row is reported as unknown rather than guessed at.",
    "",
    "One id can need different targets per family and the data layout is the same",
    "for all of them, so the layouts live in \"variant_sets\" and each family is",
    "one line. If a pasted staircase climbs the wrong way, the set is the single",
    "place to fix it."
  ],

  "variant_sets": {
    "_comment": [
      "The legacy data layout for a shape, shared by every material. Stairs: bits",
      "0-1 are east/west/south/north and bit 2 flips the stair over; data 2 is the",
      "side the full-height half faces. This game names a stair by the side its step",
      "rises toward and calls the northward one the plain block, so data 3 maps to",
      "the bare name."
    ],

    "stair_data": {
      "0": "{family}_e",
      "1": "{family}_w",
      "2": "{family}_s",
      "3": "{family}",
      "4": "{family}_e_up",
      "5": "{family}_w_up",
      "6": "{family}_s_up",
      "7": "{family}_n_up"
    },

    "_comment_slabs": [
      "Slabs: bit 3 is the top half. The stone slab's low bits are the material",
      "(0 stone, 3 cobblestone) and the wooden slab's are the species, so the two",
      "cannot share one set."
    ],
    "stone_slab_data": {
      "0": "{family}",
      "3": "cobblestone",
      "8": "{family}_top",
      "11": "cobblestone"
    },
    "double_stone_slab_data": {
      "0": "{family}",
      "3": "cobblestone"
    }
  },

